  "title": "U.S. Growth Hit a 4.3% Pace. Why Does It Still Feel Expensive?",
  "deck": "The economy grew faster than first estimated from July through September. In October, consumer prices were 3.8% higher than a year earlier and inflation-adjusted spending barely moved.",
  "category": "economy",
  "categoryLabel": "Economy & Energy",
